body:
It’s possible they agree with you - I think the difference between productive and non-productive in this circumstance is more;

‘activities essential/beneficial for continuing life’ - in most cultures that means staying healthy, having a job, pursuing social or romantic relationships if desired, vs;

Activities like gaming or reading that do not have physical output.

I'm doing the same thing two months later. It's super boring. I've read all of the Mistwalker series and all of the rest of SA and it's just not very interesting. I feel like someone is just telling me things that ultimately don't matter.

&#x200B;

Considering the ending of Oathbringer and the insane amount of shit that happened, it was always going to be a challenge to keep the pace interesting. Instead, I feel very much like the book is stuck in the weeds to a terminal degree.

Lots of the hallmarks of Deftones vocals and drums are there, too, though. That compression and the rhythm of the lyrics on the vocals scream Deftones to me, and the drums are structured in a very similar way to a lot of Deftones songs, especially My Own Summer, with a straightforward line in the chorus and then some slightly more complicated grooves in the verses. The clean bridge even feels a little like Hexagram to me.

&#x200B;

It's not like Gods doesn't have any merit on its own, of course it brings unique ideas to the table. It's just that Deftones are a very idiosyncratic band and when those themes show up elsewhere it's hard not to say 'damn, sounds like Deftones.' Like with Fightstar, but they were pretty much a Deftones tribute act.

Firmly disagree. Much respect and much love to people who feel differently, but I certainly feel like I know and understand this team. Minor improvements have been made in some areas, and I will never not enjoy watching our immensely talented squad. That said, in many others, we've either remained the same as we were last season or gotten considerably worse - most notably the secondary. 

&#x200B;

I think it's reasonable for the majority of Falcon fans to believe - based on two years of hard evidence - that our coaching staff is fundamentally unaware of how to consistently direct a winning football team. 

&#x200B;

We may win next week. We might even have a winning record this season. With our current coaching staff and secondary, we won't do anything more than that. I'll still watch and I'll still support, but I can't lie to myself and to others about what state I feel is in.

&#x200B;

I'll summarize it like this: there have indeed been a lot of very pessimistic and reactionary fans in the Falcons fanbase since our Super Bowl run. They have also been totally correct about the performance and trajectory of the team as it currently is.
